<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thaenae</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Thyna</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thaenae was an ancient port town on the eastern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, just south of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sfax">Sfax</a>, at the site now called Thyna. It marked the eastern end of the fossa regia, the ditch separating the Roman province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> from Numidia, and later lay in the province of Byzacena. Excavations have revealed baths, houses and mosaics.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thaenae.jpg" alt="Thaenae" width="320" height="187" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: El Golli Mohamed · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thyna.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
